<task id="120" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Bring the Office route surface inside RouteAuthorizationGuardTests — classify it, teach the guard the three filter names it cannot see, and record the gaps that surfaces as Pending waivers</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-29, session 25; inbound handover GitHub #1015 from spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1, owner-approved)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies tests/** (TEST-MODIFYING override row, root CLAUDE.md §8, forces code-review + adr-check unconditionally) AND modifies .cs on an authorization filter. Tags include auth.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive. The central judgement is which of three filter names counts as a per-resource gate; crediting the wrong one produces a guard that reports green over eight ungated routes, which is strictly worse than the blind spot it replaces.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs is a single 1849-line file edited in four separate regions by this task; also edits Api/Filters/JobOwnershipFilter.cs and Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
